1. Terraform Modules
    - A module is a container for multiple Terraform resources that are used together. Modules help organize code, improve reusability, and reduce duplication.
    - Every Terraform configuration is technically a module:
        Root Module → The Terraform configuration in your current working directory.
        Child Module → A module called by another module using a module block.

2. Typical Module Structure
    modules/
    └── vpc/
        ├── main.tf
        ├── variables.tf
        ├── outputs.tf
        └── README.md
    File	        Purpose
    main.tf	        Resources and module logic
    variables.tf	Input variables
    outputs.tf	    Values exposed to callers
    README.md	    Documentation

3. Creating a Module
    modules/vpc/variables.tf
        variable "vpc_cidr" {
            type = string
        }
        variable "name" {
            type = string
        }
    modules/vpc/main.tf
        resource "aws_vpc" "this" {
            cidr_block = var.vpc_cidr
            tags = {
                Name = var.name
            }
        }
    modules/vpc/outputs.tf
        output "vpc_id" {
            value = aws_vpc.this.id
        }
    
    - Calling a Module
        module "vpc" {
            source = "./modules/vpc"
            vpc_cidr = "10.0.0.0/16"
            name     = "my-vpc"
        }
    - Access module outputs:
        output "vpc_id" {
            value = module.vpc.vpc_id
        }

4. Module Sources
    - Terraform can load modules from different locations.
    Source Type	Example
    Local Path	        ./modules/vpc
    Terraform Registry	terraform-aws-modules/vpc/aws
    GitHub	            github.com/org/repo//modules/vpc
    Git (SSH)	        git::ssh://git@github.com/org/repo.git
    Git (HTTPS)	        git::https://github.com/org/repo.git
    S3 Archive	        s3::https://bucket.s3.amazonaws.com/modules/vpc.zip

5. Using Registry Modules
    - Example:
        module "vpc" {
            source  = "terraform-aws-modules/vpc/aws"
            version = "5.0.0"
            name = "my-vpc"
            cidr = "10.0.0.0/16"
            azs             = ["us-east-1a", "us-east-1b"]
            private_subnets = ["10.0.1.0/24", "10.0.2.0/24"]
            public_subnets  = ["10.0.101.0/24", "10.0.102.0/24"]
        }

6. Benefits of Modules
    - Code Reusability: Write once, use many times.
    - Consistency: Standardized infrastructure across environments.
    - Maintainability: Changes made in one place propagate everywhere.
    - Abstraction: Consumers don't need to know implementation details.
    - Team Collaboration: Different teams can own different modules.